-- ---------- 3. aero ----------
-- 963 stage 2c: aero + speed figures. The stage-1 clone carried the Lotus Exige WTA's aero block (drag 361.4, drag
-- scale 1.149, downforce 320/576), which cost ~30 mph of top speed vs Forza Motorsport (user, 2026-09-26).
-- Rule = what PG did on the 339 cars shipped in both FM and FH6 (notes/import-as-new.md s.34):
--   BodyAeroLongitudinalDrag  = FM x 0.70 (median 0.700; 121 carried 1:1, the re-tuned rest cluster at 0.69-0.70)
--   GameDragScale             = 1.0        (178/339, and every prototype analogue)
--   BodyAeroLateralDragFront/Rear, BodyAeroWIForceScale = carried from FM (316/339, 262/339 identical)
--   BodyAeroForwardDownforceFront/Rear = FM x 1.08 / x 1.36 (the two LMP analogues 787B and Furai: 1.08/1.36, 1.08/1.35;
--                               all 8 prototype analogues: medians 1.08 / 1.55) - PG re-authors these by hand: DECLARED STOPGAP
--   Front/RearDownforceClampKG = downforce x 3.93 / x 3.32 (medians over 143 FH6 cars with positive downforce: 3.90 / 3.36)
--   TopSpeed-mph (display)    = FM value (245/339 identical);  SimTopSpeed = FM value (ratio ~0.99)
--   GameTorqueScale stays 1.0 (FM 0.9 -> FH6 1.0 on every prototype analogue). TireAeroHack* keep the FH6 convention 0/5/5.
-- FM source row: por_5_963_23 (Id 3876): drag 225.8903, lateral 220/280, downforce 236/354, WI 0.656, TopSpeed 212, SimTopSpeed 95.032829
UPDATE [Data_Car] SET
  [BodyAeroLongitudinalDrag]=158.1232,
  [GameDragScale]=1.0,
  [BodyAeroLateralDragFront]=220.0,
  [BodyAeroLateralDragRear]=280.0,
  [BodyAeroWIForceScale]=0.656,
  [BodyAeroForwardDownforceFront]=254.88,
  [BodyAeroForwardDownforceRear]=481.44,
  [FrontDownforceClampKG]=1001.6784,
  [RearDownforceClampKG]=1598.3808,
  [TopSpeed-mph]=212.0,
  [SimTopSpeed]=95.032829
WHERE [Id]=9501;

